  "itemGroup.assortedtools": "Assorted Tools",
  "key.assortedtools.tool_switch_modes": "Switch Tool Modes",
  "key.category.assortedtools.general": "Assorted Tools",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.armor": "Armor",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.armor.armor": "A full four piece set for every material this mod adds tools for, on the same ladder the tools use.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.armor.armor.title": "Armor Sets",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.armor.chicken_suit": "The chicken suit is not about protection. Every piece you are wearing gives you one more jump in the air, so the full set is four jumps.\n\nIt is not flying. It is close enough to get across most things, and to get you down off most of the rest safely.\n\nTry combining them with the corresponding piece in an Anvil to see what happens.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.armor.chicken_suit.title": "Chicken Suit",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.buckets": "Buckets",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.buckets.buckets": "These buckets hold more than one bucket of what is in them, and the material decides how many.\n\nSome materials are very weak and are destroyed when they are emptied. \n\nHotter fluids need a sturdier bucket, so what a bucket can pick up is a question of material as well.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.buckets.buckets.title": "Better Buckets",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.buckets.milk": "Any of these buckets can be used to milk cows.\n\nWhat you can milk depends on the bucket. All of them can manage a cow, better ones also manage a sheep, and the best of them a pig as well.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.buckets.milk.title": "Milking",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.pokeball": "Pokeball",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.pokeball.pokeball": "Throw a pokeball at a mob and it goes inside, exactly as it was. So health, name, anything it was carrying. Throw it again and the mob comes back out.\n\nA hostile mob let out of a pokeball is still hostile, and still remembers you so be careful.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.pokeball.pokeball.title": "Pokeball",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs": "Staffs",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.frost": "The blaze rod's cold counterpart. Strays drop them as blazes drop theirs, and any other monster killed in a snowy biome sometimes does.\n\nA frost rod grinds into frost powder, and frost powder, gunpowder and a snowball make ice charges.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.frost.title": "Frost Rods",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.neptune": "Switch its mode with the tool mode key, Z by default.\n\nPlace Water pours a water source where you click. Freeze Mobs freezes every mob around you solid, and Freeze Water turns the still water around you to ice.\n\nIt is no weapon, but anything it hits is frozen where it stands.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.neptune.title": "Neptune Staff",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.phoenix": "The Neptune staff's the opposite. Place Lava and Place Fire where you click, Thaw Mobs frees every frozen mob around you, and Melt Ice melts the ice around you.\n\nA hit with it thaws a frozen mob.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.phoenix.title": "Phoenix Staff",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.power": "Right click a block to push it one step away, or in a pull mode to drag it one step toward the side you clicked.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.staffs.power.title": "Power Staff",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools": "Tools",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.basic": "Pickaxe, axe, shovel, hoe and sword, in every material. They behave exactly as the vanilla ones do.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.basic.title": "The Basic Set",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.hammers": "A hammer destroys a block in one hit and drops nothing at all.\n\nBe careful where you use it but they can come in handy.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.hammers.title": "Hammers",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.machetes": "A machete is a lighter, quicker sword that cuts through leaves, vines, wool, cactus and the rest of the undergrowth.\n\nThey come in every material, from wood up to netherite.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.machetes.title": "Machetes",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.materials": "Every metal and gem Assorted Core adds gets a full tool set here, so tin, silver, bronze, steel, ruby and the rest of them.\n\nVanilla's own materials are not repeated as pickaxes and swords, since the game already has those. They do turn up in the tools vanilla has no version of though like hammers, multitools, shears, spears and buckets all go from wood up to netherite.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.materials.title": "Materials",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.multitools": "A multitool is a sword, pickaxe, axe, shovel and hoe in one slot, and mines all of them at its material's speed.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.multitools.title": "Multitools",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.portable_workbench": "A crafting table you can carry. Right click with it to craft on the spot.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.portable_workbench.title": "Portable Workbench",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.shears": "Shears in every material, from wood up to netherite. Also lookout for a new Shears enchantment that lets you harvest coral without needing Silk Touch.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.tools.shears.title": "Shears",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.ultimate": "The Ultimate Fist",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.ultimate.fist": "All eight fragments and a nether star make the ultimate fist. It is extremely powerful and out of the box it mines very fast and hits hard enough to kill most things in one hit.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.ultimate.fist.title": "The Ultimate Fist",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.ultimate.fragments": "Eight fragments of something an older civilization built, found in chests across Minecraft.\n\nLaid out in order they spell out what they came from.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.ultimate.fragments.title": "Fragments",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands": "Wands",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.basic": "Three wands. The building wand puts up boxes, frames, rooms and lines of torches. The mining wand clears wood, dirt or ore. The breaking wand takes everything out, or leaves the ores where they are if you ask it to.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.basic.title": "Basic Wands",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.modes": "Each wand has several modes and you switch between them with the mode keybind, Z by default.\n\nA wand works on a region rather than a block, so it will tell you when you have picked too much, when the corners do not match, or when you do not have the blocks to finish the job. Nothing happens until it can be done properly.\n\nWands have a limited number of uses.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.modes.title": "How Wands Work",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.reinforced": "The reinforced version of each wand lasts far longer and unlocks the modes the basic one refuses.\n\nFilling a cave, flooding a space with water, or pouring lava into one, and surface mining, all need a reinforced wand.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.wands.reinforced.title": "Reinforced Wands",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons": "Thrown Weapons",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.boomerangs": "A boomerang is thrown with right click, flies out to its limit and comes back to you. It hurts what it passes through on the way.\n\nThe diamond one goes further and hits harder, and can be set to follow where you are looking rather than flying straight.\n\nThey might even pickup some items on the way.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.boomerangs.title": "Boomerangs",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.spears": "These spears act exactly like the Vanilla spears in Minecraft but in all of the different materials we support.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.spears.title": "Spears",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.throwing_spears": "A throwing spear is thrown with right click and sticks where it lands, ready to be picked back up.\n\nThey come in every material and also make sure you checkout the enchantment table for some fun with these.",
  "manual.assortedtools.chapter.weapons.throwing_spears.title": "Throwing Spears",
  "manual.assortedtools.description": "Tool and armor sets for every material, buckets that hold more than one, throwing weapons and the wands that do the digging for you.",
  "manual.assortedtools.title": "Assorted Tools",
  "result.wand.fill": "%s blocks filled up with stone.",
  "result.wand.mine": "No ores found.",
